    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d718">

                <pb facs="0835" n="717" xml:id="pg717"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">660f.116Auto/46: Telegram</note>
                <head><hi rendition="#italic">The Minister in Czechoslovakia</hi> (<hi rendition="#italic">Einstein</hi>) <hi
                        rendition="#italic">to the Secretary of
                    State</hi></head>
                <opener><dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >Prague</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1929-02-02T12:00:00+01:00"><hi rendition="#italic">02, February
                                1929—noon</hi>.</date><lb/>[Received February 2—9:10
                        a.m.]</dateline></opener>
                <p>13. Legation’s despatch No. 1689, December 6, 1928.<anchor n="56"
                        xml:id="d718-f1"/> Foreign Office note informs Legation confidentially that
                    American motor contingent will be increased from 800 to 1500 cars. Kindly
                    refrain from publicity.<anchor n="57" xml:id="d718-f2"/></p>
                <closer><signed><hi rendition="#small-caps">Einstein</hi></signed></closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
    <standOff>
        <listAnnotation>
            <note corresp="#d718-f1" n="56" xml:id="d718-f1-content">
                <p>Not printed.</p>
            </note>
            <note corresp="#d718-f2" n="57" xml:id="d718-f2-content">
                <p>American automobile interests were given permission to receive this information
                    in confidence; telegram 17, Feb. 28, 1929, from the Chargé in Czechoslovakia to
                    the Secretary of State (file No. 660f.116 Auto/53).</p>
            </note>
        </listAnnotation>
    </standOff>
